## 1. Transformation Input and Processing Specification

### 1.1 Input Source

This stage receives the **approved extraction handover**. It does not read the source CSV files and does not re-extract. The source system and the extraction contract are described in the Stage 1 documentation and are not repeated here.

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Input name | Approved extraction handover package (Stage 1 output) |
| Contents | (1) DataFrames `stocks`, `sales`, `expenses`; (2) extraction run metadata (run ID, timestamps, source filenames, extraction window, row counts per domain); (3) extraction validation summary |
| Format | pandas DataFrames passed in memory by Prefect inside the same `@flow`. Every column is text (`string`). |
| Persisted copy | On APPROVED, Extraction also writes the handover to `staging/<parent_run_id>/` as UTF-8 CSV (`stocks.csv`, `sales.csv`, `expenses.csv`) plus `extraction_metadata.json` and `extraction_validation_summary.csv`. Transform reads this copy only when a batch is restarted (see 1.2). |
| Extraction run ID | `parent_run_id`, e.g. `run_20261011_000000` |
| Batch window | The previous calendar day, e.g. `2026-10-10 00:00:00` to `2026-10-10 23:59:59` (Asia/Manila) |
| Entry condition | Extraction status is `APPROVED` (automatically, or after the Owner approved a MANUAL REVIEW hold) |
| State of the input | Headers already in snake_case; only the batch window kept; source `total_amount` already removed; **all values still text**, so this stage owns every type conversion |

**Example.** Extraction run `run_20261011_000000` stages the records of 2026-10-10 for `stocks`, `sales`, and `expenses`. Stage 2 receives them, profiles them, applies the cleaning, standardization, and business rules, validates the result, and hands the transformed tables to Load as batch `BATCH_20261010` under transformation run `TRN_20261011_000000`.

### 1.2 Batch Processing Method

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Technology | Python 3 with pandas; one Prefect `@task` (`transform_batch`) inside the extraction `@flow` |
| Schedule | No separate schedule. Runs immediately after extraction, which runs **daily at 00:00 (Asia/Manila)**. |
| Batch window / size | All records in the handover for the previous calendar day. Daily volume is small, so the whole batch is processed in memory. |
| Batch ID | `BATCH_<YYYYMMDD of the window date>`, e.g. `BATCH_20261010`. It stays the same on every rerun of that window. |
| Run ID | `TRN_<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS of the start>`; a new run ID is created on every attempt. |
| Limits | One active run, 3 retries on transient errors, 30-minute timeout |
| Output | Transformed DataFrames, transformation metadata, and validation summary passed to Load. Row data is written to `staging/transformed/<batch_id>/`; metadata and validation results to `audit/`. |

**Failed batch restart**

1. **Transient error** (file lock, `blockflow.db` lookup temporarily unavailable): Prefect retries the task up to 3 times. Each retry restarts from the beginning of `transform_batch` using the same input.
2. **Task failed or timed out after retries:** the run is marked `REJECTED`, nothing is handed to Load, and the error code is logged. After the cause is fixed, the Owner starts the flow in *transform-only* mode with the `parent_run_id`. Transform then reads the persisted copy in `staging/<parent_run_id>/`. Extraction is **not** run again.
3. **Source data problem** (e.g. many rejected rows): the Owner corrects the source file and re-runs the whole window from Extraction, which creates a new extraction run and a new handover.

**Idempotency: yes.** Transform is a pure function of its input and the versioned rules. It keeps no state between runs. Running the same batch twice gives the same transformed rows. Outputs are written per `batch_id`: a rerun **replaces** the files in `staging/transformed/<batch_id>/`, `rejected/` (same batch ID), and the audit summary for that batch. It never appends to them, so no duplicates are created. Stage 3 must load with an upsert on the primary key so that a rerun does not duplicate rows in `blockflow.db`.

### 1.3 Transformation Scope

| Table | Cleaned | Standardized | Derived | Aggregated |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `stocks` | all columns (C-01 to C-10) | `stock_id`, `size`, `quantity`, `unit`, `unit_price`, `updated_at`, `recorded_by` | none | none |
| `sales` | all columns (C-01 to C-10) | `sale_id`, `customer_name`, `phone_number`, `shop_name`, `quantity`, `unit_price`, `sale_date`, `recorded_by`, `stock_id` | `total_amount` (B-01) | none |
| `expenses` | all columns (C-01 to C-10) | `expense_id`, `category`, `description`, `amount`, `expense_date`, `recorded_by` | none | none |

**Out of scope:** reading CSV files (Extraction), writing to `blockflow.db` (Load), the `users` table, external data such as competitor pricing, and loading, indexing, or performance tuning.

### 1.4 Dependencies and Assumptions

**Processing order**

| Order | Table | Why |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | Reference data (read-only): `users.user_id` list and existing `stocks.stock_id` list from `blockflow.db`; `config/reference_values.csv` | Needed for orphan checks (C-08) and code mapping (S-06, S-07) |
| 1 | `stocks` | `sales.stock_id` refers to it; stocks received in the same batch count as valid parents |
| 2 | `sales` | Depends on cleaned `stocks` |
| 3 | `expenses` | Independent of the other tables |

**Assumptions**

| ID | Assumption | If it does not hold |
|---|---|---|
| A-01 | Extraction writes the persisted copy (1.1) | Restart is impossible; update Stage 1 |
| A-02 | Times are local (Asia/Manila), no conversion | Wrong time stored |
| A-03 | Transform only reads key lists from `blockflow.db`; `users` is not transformed | Run stops (`TRF-E03`) |
| A-04 | Owner maintains `config/reference_values.csv` | Run stops (V-01) |
| A-05 | Late records belong to an already processed window | Owner re-runs that date |
| A-06 | `sales_id` and `expenses_id` are accepted as aliases (S-10) | V-02 fails |
| A-07 | Load upserts on the primary key | Reruns could duplicate rows |
| A-08 | Thresholds and reference lists are initial values | Owner confirms; a change is a new rules version |

