## 3. Data Cleaning Rules

**No record is dropped silently.** Every rejected row is written to the rejected area with its `batch_id`, `rule_id`, and reason (Section 9) and is counted in the metadata (Section 8). A record that is cleaned and kept is *modified*, not rejected.

### 3.1 Rules

| Rule ID | Target | Condition | Action | Justification |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| C-01 | All text columns | Extra spaces, control or zero-width characters | Trim, collapse spaces, remove characters | Avoids false mismatches |
| C-02 | All columns | Empty, blank, or `N/A`, `NULL`, `NONE`, `-` | Convert to null | One definition of "missing" |
| C-03 | Required columns (note 1) | Null after C-02 or failed conversion | **Reject** | Keys, money, and dates are never invented |
| C-04 | `sales.customer_name`, `shop_name`, `phone_number` | Null | Fill `Unknown` | The sale is still valid |
| C-05 | `expenses.description` | Null | Fill `No description` | The expense is still valid |
| C-06 | `quantity`, `unit_price`, `amount` | Zero or negative | **Reject** | Invalid business value |
| C-07 | `quantity`, `unit_price`, `amount` | Above the outlier limit (note 2) | Keep and flag | A person decides, not the pipeline |
| C-08 | `recorded_by`, `sales.stock_id` | Key has no parent (note 3) | **Reject** | Prevents broken links |
| C-09 | All three tables | Identical business columns after cleaning (note 4) | Keep lowest ID; log the rest as duplicates | The first entry is the original |
| C-10 | `updated_at`, `sale_date`, `expense_date` | Parsed date outside the batch window | **Reject** | Catches day/month swaps |

**Notes**

1. **C-03 required columns:** all IDs and `recorded_by`; `sales.stock_id`; `stocks.size`, `quantity`, `unit`, `unit_price`, `updated_at`; `sales.quantity`, `unit_price`, `sale_date`; `expenses.category`, `amount`, `expense_date`. Reasons: `null_required` or `unparseable_value`.
2. **C-07 limits (configurable):** `quantity` above 10,000; `unit_price` above 1,000.00; `amount` above 100,000.00. Checked by V-15.
3. **C-08 parents:** `recorded_by` must be in `users.user_id`. `sales.stock_id` must be in existing `stocks.stock_id` or in the stocks of this batch.
4. **C-09 comparison:** all columns except the `_id` column. Dropped rows go to the rejected area as `duplicate` and are counted as `duplicates_dropped`.

### 3.2 Execution Order

1. C-01 text cleanup, then C-02 null normalization
2. Type conversion and standardization (S-01 to S-10); a failed conversion becomes null
3. C-03 required-value rejects, then C-04 and C-05 fills
4. C-06 invalid values, then C-10 window check
5. C-08 orphan check (after `stocks` is cleaned, so same-batch stocks are valid parents)
6. C-09 duplicate removal
7. C-07 outlier flag
8. B-01 derivation (Section 5)

A row rejected at an earlier step is not processed by later steps and is counted once, under the first rule that rejected it.

### 3.3 Required Considerations: Where Each Is Handled

| Consideration | Rule(s) |
|---|---|
| Missing or null values (default, fill, or reject) | C-02, C-03 (reject), C-04, C-05 (fill) |
| Duplicates and which record is kept | C-09 (lowest ID kept) |
| Whitespace and invalid characters | C-01 |
| Invalid, out-of-range values and outliers | C-06 (reject), C-07 (flag), C-10 |
| Orphan records | C-08 |

