### 6.2 Naming Convention 
Table and column names use snake_case with complete words and no unclear abbreviations. Table names are lowercase and plural (stocks, sales, expenses, users). No dim_, fact_, or stg_ prefixes appear in the output, because the output is operational tables; staging copies are kept in folders named for the run and batch, not in table names.
A primary key is the singular table name plus _id: stock_id, sale_id, expense_id. Stage 1 uses the same singular spelling; source files that spell them sales_id or expenses_id are accepted as aliases and renamed by this stage (S-10). A foreign key keeps the name of the key it references (stock_id); the exception is recorded_by, named for its role, which references users.user_id. Date fields use _date for event dates and _at for last-update timestamps. No surrogate keys (_key) are generated.

 
