### Schema Consistency        
Schema Consistency defines how the BlockFlow ETL pipeline detects, handles, and responds to unexpected changes in the input schema—such as altered column names, changed data types, missing required fields, or added columns—before any batch is accepted into the pipeline. This ensures that structural drift in the source CSV files never silently corrupts downstream data.      


### 7. Transformation Validation and Data Quality Checks 
This section defines the checks used to verify that the transformed data is correct, complete, and suitable for loading into blockflow.db. Each check is executed inside the Prefect transformation flow after cleaning, using the validated dataset handed over from the Extraction Stage. Together, the checks verify the integrity, correctness, completeness, and business rule compliance of the transformed output, not source connectivity or extraction completeness, which belong to the Extraction Stage. 


| ID   | Check Name                           | Target                           | Purpose                             | Validation Criteria                                                   | Severity     |
| ---- | ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |
| V-01 | Handover and dependency readiness    | Extraction metadata, lookups     | Baseline for reconciliation         | Status APPROVED; read count equals extraction count; lookups readable | Critical     |
| V-02 | Input schema match                   | Input columns                    | Detect source format changes        | All expected columns present                                          | Critical     |
| V-03 | Output schema and format conformance | Each output table                | Load receives the exact contract    | Types, formats, lengths match Section 6                               | Critical     |
| V-04 | Required values present              | NOT NULL columns                 | No nulls after transformation       | Null count = 0                                                        | Critical     |
| V-05 | Primary key uniqueness               | stock_id, sale_id, expense_id    | Prevent duplicate keys              | Duplicate keys = 0                                                    | Critical     |
| V-06 | Duplicate business records           | Each output table                | Prevent inflated totals             | Duplicate rows = 0                                                    | Critical     |
| V-07 | Referential integrity                | sales.stock_id, recorded_by      | Prevent orphans                     | 100% of keys have a parent                                            | Critical     |
| V-08 | Business rules and total accuracy    | Quantities, prices, total_amount | Valid values, correct derived field | Values valid; total_amount = quantity × unit_price (2 dp)             | Critical     |
| V-09 | Record reconciliation                | Each table                       | Detect lost records                 | read = output + rejected + duplicates                                 | Critical     |
| V-10 | Aggregate reconciliation             | Quantity and amount sums         | Removals did not change measures    | Sum in = out + rejected + duplicates                                  | Critical     |
| V-11 | Lookup cardinality                   | B-02, B-03 lookups               | Detect row multiplication           | Row count unchanged by lookups                                        | Critical     |
| V-12 | Rejected log completeness            | rejected/ files                  | Nothing dropped silently            | Rows in file = rejected + duplicates                                  | Critical     |
| V-13 | Output not lost                      | Each output table                | Detect a wiped-out table            | Output > 0 when input > 0                                             | Critical     |
| V-14 | Rejection rate                       | Each table                       | Detect export faults                | Rejected share ≤ 5%                                                   | Non-critical |
| V-15 | Outlier review                       | Quantity and money columns       | Person confirms unusual values      | Flagged outliers = 0                                                  | Non-critical |
| V-16 | Unexpected input columns             | Input columns                    | Notice source changes               | No extra columns                                                      | Non-critical |

### 8. Transformation Metadata and Log Specification 
This section defines the metadata and log records required to monitor, trace, and audit each transformation batch run in the BlockFlow ETL pipeline. For every batch, the pipeline captures run identifiers, batch context, record counts, rules applied, validation results, error diagnostics, execution timing, and code version enabling full observability and reliable recovery from the transformation stage through to loading.

